// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 04-expressions/mut_string_length_fold_capability_neg_01.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A `mut` string binding may be written after its declaration, so the folded
// byte length of its literal initializer is not necessarily the value the
// `.length` read observes. The checker keeps the runtime-member drain and the
// HIR shape resolver rejects the fold for a mutable binding, so the body fails
// closed with ZOM4099 instead of returning a stale constant or reaching a
// missing-fact invariant.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/04-expressions/mut_string_length_fold_capability_neg_01.zom:4:12
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |
// CHECK-LITERAL: 4 |     return s.length;
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |            ^~~~~~~~
// CHECK-LITERAL: 1 error generated.
